<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Prayer times — THE prayer-times entry, after the phase 0 merge.

  It used to be "Day at a glance" and sat next to "All prayer times", which
  were two picker entries for one idea: the same six times, the same payload,
  a different stylesheet. `selectLayout` already chose the layout from
  measured size rather than from the provider class, which is what made one
  entry possible — drag this narrow and it is the strip, drag it tall and it
  is the list with the night times, drag it to four rows and the practice
  graph comes with it.

  So the range is deliberately wide: 4x1 up to 4x4, and it means something
  different at each end. `targetCellHeight` is 1 because that is what the
  content actually needs: the six times are one row of columns, and the
  header the second row was paying for is the city — the line you can most
  afford to lose. Placed at one row it draws the times and what is next;
  drag it to two and the location and the Hijri date come back; three
  brings the practice graph and four the month footer. Every row you give
  it buys something, which is not true of a widget that starts at the size
  it ends at.

  `maxResizeHeight` is 600dp, not the 400 it was, because 400 was smaller
  than a size this widget actually reaches. 400 reads like four rows times
  the nominal 100dp a row, but a launcher row is not 100dp of widget — the
  gaps between rows belong to the widget too, and a row is only 100dp at
  one particular density. On a 1080x2400 emulator at 420dpi the card
  measures 99dp at one row, 210 at two, 321 at three and 432 at four; drop
  the same device to 300dpi, which is what a user with a large display size
  gets, and three rows alone is 488dp. Declaring a 400dp maximum for a card
  the launcher is already drawing at 488 is just false, and it is the
  practice footer — the band that opens at 375dp — that a low ceiling
  strands. 600dp covers four rows at every cell height a phone or tablet is
  likely to hand us.

  Worth knowing before touching the band constants: at 420dpi a Pixel-style
  4x6 grid tops this widget out at three rows, so 321dp is all it ever gets
  there and the footer only appears on roomier configurations. Both bands
  were rendered and checked, the 265-375 one at 420dpi and the 375-up one at
  300dpi; neither clips.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:configure="com.prayer_times.PrayerWidgetConfigureActivity"
    android:description="@string/widget_description_prayer_times"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/prayer_widget_strip"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="60dp"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/prayer_widget_strip_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="60dp"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:maxResizeWidth="500dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="600dp" />

